  "summary": "Ken Livingstone was re-elected Mayor of London, this time as the official Labour candidate after rejoining the party he had left to run as an independent in 2000. He won 685,541 first-preference votes (36.8%) and was returned with 828,380 votes (55.4%) after second preferences, ahead of Conservative Steve Norris on 667,178 (44.6%). The Conservatives became the largest Assembly party with nine seats, and UKIP won its first two Assembly seats. This was the first London election to feature an official London Elects candidate booklet.",
